eDOCr2-pytorch is eDOCr2 ported to PyTorch, without TensorFlow. It contains, or depends on, the works below; each
is under the MIT License, whose text is in LICENSE.

eDOCr2 - https://github.com/javvi51/edocr2
    Copyright (c) 2024 javvi51 (Javier Villena Toro, Design Automation Lab, Linkoping University).
    The segmentation and OCR pipeline in edocr2/tools/ is eDOCr2's. eDOCr2's two recognizers
    (release v1.0.0) are read from that release; eDOCr2-pytorch does not redistribute them.
    eDOCr2 succeeds eDOCr (https://github.com/javvi51/eDOCr) by the same author.

keras-ocr - https://github.com/faustomorales/keras-ocr
    Fausto Morales.
    edocr2/ocr_utils.py (box decoding, image fitting) is taken from keras-ocr, which eDOCr and
    eDOCr2 include, and the recognizer in edocr2/models/crnn.py reproduces keras-ocr's network.

CRAFT - https://github.com/clovaai/CRAFT-pytorch
    Copyright (c) 2019-present NAVER Corp.
    The text detector, used through the craft-detector package
    (https://github.com/wkpark/CRAFT-pytorch). Its weights, craft_mlt_25k.pth, trained on
    SynthText, IC13 and IC17, are fetched from that package's release v0.0.2, which holds the file
    of CRAFT's original download, and are not redistributed by eDOCr2-pytorch.
